[110.063, "o", "{\"advice\":\"Since you prefer mornings and don't like swimming, try a morning routine with brisk walking, mall walking on hazy days, or a short home circuit. For you, a safe start is 10-15 min easy walk after breakfast, then build up slowly. Add 2+ days a week of simple strength work like sit-to-stand and wall push-ups, plus a little balance work near support. Because your region is hazy and you have elevated blood glucose and high screening risk, keep outdoor exercise lighter on poor-air days and choose indoor options. Also, please follow up your high screening result with a doctor.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"supporting_guides\":[\"lg-06-exercise-by-condition\",\"lg-09-hazy-day-activity\",\"lg-10-active-after-60\",\"lg-02-physical-activity-guideline\",\"lg-08-screening-schedule\"],\"rationale\":\"This fits your profile: age 60-64, elevated blood glucose, low steps and MVPA, North/Woodlands, and hazy conditions. The guides support morning activity, indoor alternatives on hazy days, gradual build-up, and adding strength and balance. High-risk screening should be followed up with a doctor.\",\"personalisation_flags\":[\"age_60_plus\",\"elevated_blood_glucose\",\"high_screening_risk\",\"low_steps\",\"low_mvpa\",\"region_hazy\",\"prefers_mornings\",\"dislikes_swimming\"]}\r\n"]
[110.063, "o", "waiting for the preference to reach memory (up to 2 minutes) ...\r\n"]
