[206.219, "o", "[livewell-abc-coach v1] 39.0s  tools: get_citizen_profile, memory:search_call, livewell-nutrition, livewell-activity, memory:search_call, memory:search_call  model: gpt-5.4-mini\r\n"]
[206.219, "o", "{\"advice\":\"Sure Rahim - keep meals simple and steady for glucose: use the plate guide each meal, with 1/2 veg, 1/4 wholegrain or sensible staple, 1/4 protein. Here's a simple week:\\n\\n**Meal plan**\\n- **Mon:** Oats + egg; brown-rice economy rice with 2 veg and fish; tofu-vegetable soup.\\n- **Tue:** Wholemeal toast + egg/tomato; fish soup with vegetables; brown rice, chicken and greens.\\n- **Wed:** Plain yoghurt + fruit; yong tau foo soup with tofu, egg and vegetables; wholegrain noodles with prawns and greens.\\n- **Thu:** Oats + nuts; chapati with dhal and vegetables; steamed fish, brown rice and greens.\\n- **Fri:** Wholemeal toast + tuna; chicken rice with modest rice and extra cucumber; tofu and vegetable stir-fry.\\n- **Sat/Sun:** Repeat your preferred meals, keep sauces/gravy light.\\n\\n**Exercise plan**\\n- **Mon:** 10-minute easy indoor walk; add 5 minutes after dinner.\\n- **Tue:** Chair strength and balance, or 10 minutes of sit-to-stands and wall push-ups.\\n- **Wed:** Two 10-minute indoor walks.\\n- **Thu:** Low-impact aerobics at a talk-test pace, if you feel well.\\n- **Fri:** 10-minute indoor walk plus gentle stretching and balance near a support.\\n- **Sat:** Indoor mall walking, starting 30-45 minutes.\\n- **Sun:** Rest or easy 10-minute walk.\\n\\nBecause your screening risk is High and your region is hazy, keep activity indoors and start gently. Please also follow up with a doctor about your glucose result.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"supporting_guides\":[\"lg-01-healthy-plate\",\"l...\r\n"]
