[329.907, "o", "[livewell-abc-coach v2] 17.0s  tools: get_citizen_profile, memory:search_call, knowledge_base_retrieve, memory:search_call  model: gpt-5.4-mini\r\n"]
[329.907, "o", "{\"advice\":\"For pre-diabetes, focus on steady meals, not crash diets. Use the healthy plate: half vegetables and fruit, one quarter wholegrains or staples, and one quarter protein. Choose brown rice, oats, wholemeal bread, or wholegrain noodles more often; pair carbs with fish, chicken, tofu, eggs, beans, or lean meat. Keep portions sensible, spread carbs across the day, and swap sugary drinks for water, kopi kosong, or teh siew dai. At hawker stalls, ask for less gravy and add vegetables. Since your screening is high, please follow up with a doctor or dietitian for a personalised plan.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"supporting_guides\":[\"lg-05-eating-for-pre-diabetes\",\"lg-01-healthy-plate\",\"lg-04-salt-and-sugar-tips\",\"lg-08-screening-schedule\"],\"rationale\":\"The profile shows elevated blood glucose, high screening risk, age 60-64, and hazy region. The food guides specifically cover pre-diabetes, healthy plate portions, and reducing sugar/sauces. The screening guide says a High-risk result needs doctor follow-up, so I included that.\",\"personalisation_flags\":[\"elevated blood glucose\",\"screening risk: High\",\"age band: 60-64\",\"region: North\",\"region is hazy\",\"preferences: morning\"]}\r\n"]
[329.907, "o", "   [PASS ] lab1_prediabetes_eat on the Fabric coach: no Fabric call -- ['get_citizen_profile', 'memory:search_call', 'knowledge_base_retrieve', 'memory:search_call']\r\n"]
